**Lazy loading** (`FetchType.LAZY`):
```java
Order order = orderRepo.findById(1L).get();
// items NOT loaded yet — just order data
List<OrderItem> items = order.getItems(); // NOW items are loaded (separate SELECT)
```

**Eager loading** (`FetchType.EAGER`):
```java
Order order = orderRepo.findById(1L).get();
// Both order AND items loaded in one JOIN query
List<OrderItem> items = order.getItems(); // Already loaded — no extra query
```

**The problem**: You load 100 orders, then loop through them and access each order's customer:
```java
List<Order> orders = orderRepo.findAll(); // 1 query: SELECT * FROM orders
for (Order order : orders) {
    System.out.println(order.getCustomer().getName()); // 1 query PER order!
}
// Total: 1 + 100 = 101 queries!
```

**The fix with JOIN FETCH**:
```java
@Query("SELECT o FROM Order o JOIN FETCH o.customer")
List<Order> findAllWithCustomer();
// Total: 1 query with JOIN — loads orders + customers together
```

```java
// Service method — @Transactional ends here
public Order getOrder(Long id) {
    return orderRepo.findById(id).orElseThrow(); // transaction closes
}

// In controller:
Order order = orderService.getOrder(1L);
order.getItems(); // BOOM! LazyInitializationException
// Transaction is closed — can't load items anymore
```

Hibernate can't open a new connection outside the transaction to fetch the lazy items.

```java
public interface OrderRepository extends JpaRepository<Order, Long> {

    // Load orders WITH items (overrides LAZY for this query)
    @EntityGraph(attributePaths = {"items"})
    List<Order> findAll();

    // Load with items AND customer
    @EntityGraph(attributePaths = {"items", "customer"})
    @Query("SELECT o FROM Order o WHERE o.status = :status")
    List<Order> findByStatus(@Param("status") String status);
}
```

Generates `LEFT JOIN FETCH` for the specified paths — single query, no N+1.

```java
// Regular JOIN — only filters, doesn't load items
@Query("SELECT o FROM Order o JOIN o.items i WHERE i.price > 100")
List<Order> findOrdersWithExpensiveItems();
// items still LAZY — accessing items later causes extra queries

// JOIN FETCH — filters AND loads items into object
@Query("SELECT DISTINCT o FROM Order o JOIN FETCH o.items WHERE o.status = 'ACTIVE'")
List<Order> findActiveOrdersWithItems();
// items are NOW loaded — no extra queries when you access order.getItems()
```
